This is quite interesting. I don't think there's any clear and
definite way to implement this as far as I've read; there's heaps of
good ideas, and it'd be a bit hard to choose from.

I imagine something resembling the c corpse could be implemented: if
you fall in a pit while wielding it, the mirror breaks and you sustain
the luck penalty.

How would this work for monsters? Would they pick up the mirror and
not attack with it? Or would they attack and shatter the mirror?

Perhaps include a "mirror of reflection" as opposed to the normal
mirror, to keep consistency with the "mundane vs magic" tool trend.

Thanks for YAINI (yet another interesting nifty idea).

